-- title:
--   Unramifiedness of the Hecke–Galois representation outside S
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a nonzero level $N$, and a finite set $S \subseteq \mathbb{N}$; let $\mathcal{O}$ be a discrete valuation domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal, let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}$ of weight-$2$ cusp forms for $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$, and $U_q$ for $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$ — to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$, and let $T$ be a noetherian local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, complete for its maximal ideal, finite and free as an $\mathcal{O}$-module, with local structure map. Assume $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal{O}$, that $p \in S$, and that every prime divisor of $N$ lies in $S$. Let $H$ be a Hecke–Galois datum for these data: a homomorphism $\pi :$ `heckeAlgebra N 2 S` $\to T$ reducing to $\theta$ modulo the maximal ideal, with $\mathcal{O}[\operatorname{im}\pi] = T$, with every $\mathcal{O}$-valued lift of $\theta$ factoring through $\pi$ via an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $T \to \mathcal{O}$, with surjective residual structure map, together with a rank-two adically continuous Galois representation $\rho$ over $T$ whose Frobenius characteristic polynomials at primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ equal $X^2 - \pi(T_\ell)X + \ell$ and whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible. Then for every prime $q \notin S$ the representation $\rho$ is unramified at $q$: for every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $q$ is a nonunit and every $\sigma$ in the image in $\operatorname{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ of the inertia subgroup of $P$, one has $\rho(\sigma) = 1$.
--
--   This is the unramifiedness half of the standard statement attaching to a system of mod-$p$ Hecke eigenvalues a two-dimensional Galois representation over a Hecke algebra, unramified outside the bad set $S$ (the Eichler–Shimura relation together with good reduction of the relevant Jacobians away from $N$). It is used downstream when the local behaviour of $\rho$ at primes outside $S$ is needed, in particular in the analysis of the ordinary and flat conditions and in the construction of patching data for the Hecke algebra.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum_isUnramifiedAt_of_notMem.lean

import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

variable {p : ℕ} {N : ℕ} [NeZero N] {S : Finset ℕ}
  {𝒪 : Type} [CommRing 𝒪] [IsDomain 𝒪] [IsDiscreteValuationRing 𝒪]
  [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪) 𝒪]
  {θ : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 (↑S : Set ℕ) →+* IsLocalRing.ResidueField 𝒪}
  {T : Type} [CommRing T] [IsLocalRing T] [IsNoetherianRing T]
  [IsAdicComplete (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal T) T] [Algebra 𝒪 T] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap 𝒪 T)]
  [Module.Finite 𝒪 T] [Module.Free 𝒪 T]

theorem CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum.isUnramifiedAt_of_notMem (hp : p.Prime)
    (hp𝒪 : (p : 𝒪) ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal 𝒪) (hpS : p ∈ S)
    (hNS : ∀ q : ℕ, q.Prime → q ∣ N → q ∈ S)
    (H : CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum N (↑S : Set ℕ) 𝒪 θ T)
    (q : ℕ) (hq : q.Prime) (hqS : q ∉ S) :
    H.ρ.IsUnramifiedAt q := by sorry
